Abstract10
The necklace splitting problem is a classic problem in fair division with many applications, including 11
data-informed fair hash maps. We extend necklace splitting to a dynamic setting, allowing for 12
relocation, insertion, and deletion of beads. We present linear-time, optimal algorithms for the 13
two-color case that support all dynamic updates. For more than two colors, we give linear-time, 14
optimal algorithms for relocation subject to a restriction on the number of agents. Finally, we 15
propose a randomized algorithm for the two-color case that handles all dynamic updates, guarantees 16
approximate fairness with high probability, and runs in polylogarithmic time when the number of 17
agents is small. 18
