1 Introduction 27
The necklace splitting problem, first introduced by Bhatt and Leiserson [ 6], is a classic 28
combinatorial fair division problem. In this work, we extend it to a dynamic setting, enabling 29
applications such as data-informed fair hash maps and improved load-balancing among 30
multiple servers. 31
