▶Proposition 10. Tis a spanning tree of G. 350
Proof.First, we prove that Tis connected. Gis trivially connected since the necklace it 351
represents is a contiguous collection of beads. We need to show that the edges removed 352
fromGto construct Tare unnecessary for connectivity. Consider any edge removed. By 353
construction, neither endpoint is on level 1. Thus, both endpoints are joined to a node on the 354
previous level corresponding to an enclosing agent, and consequently, they remain connected. 355
Next, we prove that Tis acyclic. Assume for contradiction that there exists a cycle in T. 356
Letℓbe the lowest level represented in the cycle. Consider a node uin the cycle on level ℓ. 357
Both of its neighbors in the cycle must be on level ℓ−1. However, by construction, each 358
node is joined to at most one node on the level below it. We have a contradiction, so Tmust 359
be acyclic. Therefore, Tis a spanning tree of G. ◀ 360
