▶Lemma 12. MinNodeMaxFlow can be solved in O(k′′logk′′+k′)time onT′. 380
Proof.The edges from the source sand to the sink tmust all be saturated to produce a 381
max flow, so we can ignore both nodes. The remaining subgraph has structure identical 382
toT, and is thus a tree. We sort the sources/sinks by their level in descending order and 383
initialize a linked list of pointers to them in that order. Consider the set of nodes with excess 384
(potentially negative) flow on the highest level (other than level 1). At first, these are all 385
sources/sinks. Each of these nodes has a unique edge leading to the level below. Any valid 386
flow must have flow on these edges. We place the appropriate amount of flow on each of these 387
edges to satisfy the demands of the sources/sinks. Then we consider the new set of nodes 388
with excess flow on the highest level (other than level 1) and repeat the process, updating 389
the linked list accordingly. We terminate once all nodes not on level 1 have no excess flow. 390
In each step, the highest level with excess flow decreases, so this process must terminate. 391
If any nodes with excess flow remain, they are on level 1. Consider the leftmost such 392
node. We put flow on each edge to the right until the current node has no excess flow. Then 393
we find the new leftmost node with excess flow and repeat the process. In each step, the 394
number of nodes with excess flow decreases, so eventually no nodes will have excess flow, at 395
which point we terminate. 396
Sorting the initial list takes O(k′′logk′′)time. In the first phase, we process only the 397
nodes in the solution, and each in constant time, giving a running time of O(k′)for the 398
first phase. In the second phase, assuming the relative position of each node on level 1 is 399
stored when Tis constructed, we can find the leftmost node in O(k′)time, and after that, 400
we only process nodes in the solution, each in constant time. This gives us a running time of 401
O(k′)for the second phase. Overall, we have a running time of O(k′′logk′′+k′)for solving 402
MinNodeMaxFlow onT′. ◀ 403
